00:50:32.160 --> 00:50:32.440
Tell it.

1119
00:50:32.780 --> 00:50:33.140
Okay.

1120
00:50:33.140 --> 00:50:36.340
I apologize to everyone out there if I've already told this story.

1121
00:50:37.420 --> 00:50:38.960
So I worked for this guy.

1122
00:50:39.240 --> 00:50:40.700
I was his administrative assistant.

1123
00:50:41.000 --> 00:50:43.620
I had to go through his email, his physical mail.

1124
00:50:43.620 --> 00:50:50.480
I received all memos, inter-office memos, and he had this color-coded filing system.

1125
00:50:50.760 --> 00:50:52.580
There were something like eight different colors.

1126
00:50:53.180 --> 00:50:54.760
And red was urgent.

1127
00:50:55.020 --> 00:50:59.620
And then like the blue folder meant like executive correspondence.

1128
00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:03.820
And then the purple folder was to be signed.

1129
00:51:04.240 --> 00:51:06.480
Each folder had a different designation.

1130
00:51:07.180 --> 00:51:11.680
But there was a problem because sometimes there would be something that was like urgent

1131
00:51:11.680 --> 00:51:15.580
that was executive correspondence and needed to be signed.

1132
00:51:15.960 --> 00:51:20.380
And I asked him when I started, what do I do with a piece of mail like this?

1133
00:51:20.520 --> 00:51:21.960
Which folder do I put it in?

1134
00:51:22.140 --> 00:51:23.980
And he said, put it in all three.

1135
00:51:24.460 --> 00:51:28.040
So you had to make three copies and put it in all three?

1136
00:51:28.460 --> 00:51:28.740
Yes.

1137
00:51:28.980 --> 00:51:29.320
Ugh.

1138
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:31.240
It was insanity.

1139
00:51:31.560 --> 00:51:32.940
It was so weird.

1140
00:51:33.100 --> 00:51:36.100
And it completely reminded me of urgent A, B, D, C.

1141
00:51:36.340 --> 00:51:39.520
I feel like that man would have created a similar system.

1142
00:51:39.960 --> 00:51:40.160
Yeah.

1143
00:51:40.640 --> 00:51:42.700
You know, Jenna, you and I temped at a lot of places.

1144
00:51:42.700 --> 00:51:45.800
We had a lot of different bosses while we were struggling actresses.

1145
00:51:45.880 --> 00:51:48.640
And this episode, when I watched it, brought back so many memories

1146
00:51:48.640 --> 00:51:51.180
of just those random bosses you could have.

1147
00:51:51.180 --> 00:51:54.240
I had one who would really try to support his workers, which was great.

1148
00:51:54.600 --> 00:51:57.240
And a few of us were doing a sketch comedy show together.

1149
00:51:57.240 --> 00:51:59.760
And he came to our sketch comedy show.

1150
00:52:00.540 --> 00:52:02.700
This was one of my bosses at 1-800-DENTISt.

1151
00:52:02.940 --> 00:52:06.900
And, you know, in a sketch comedy, you play a lot of wacky characters, right?

1152
00:52:07.240 --> 00:52:07.480
Yeah.

1153
00:52:07.560 --> 00:52:09.840
And I played all kinds of crazy, wacky characters.

1154
00:52:09.960 --> 00:52:14.280
And I don't think he knew much about me because I just kind of kept to myself.

1155
00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:19.380
I would come, sit at my station, answer calls from people looking for dentists,

1156
00:52:19.440 --> 00:52:20.100
and then I'd leave.

1157
00:52:20.100 --> 00:52:25.080
But after he came to this sketch show, it's like he thought I was the crazy gal,

1158
00:52:25.500 --> 00:52:26.800
the crazy, wacky gal.

1159
00:52:27.020 --> 00:52:27.640
I was Andy.

1160
00:52:27.860 --> 00:52:28.740
You were Andy.

1161
00:52:29.120 --> 00:52:29.540
Yes.

1162
00:52:29.640 --> 00:52:30.700
And he would walk past me.

1163
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:31.940
He'd be like, she's crazy.

1164
00:52:31.940 --> 00:52:33.960
She's going to say something crazy and funny.

1165
00:52:34.180 --> 00:52:35.620
And I'd just be like, yeah.

1166
00:52:35.860 --> 00:52:38.320
And I'd be like, ah, just like the same thing.

1167
00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:41.860
So much so he would also say, I bet you know where the parties are.

1168
00:52:42.300 --> 00:52:45.420
I was like, I don't know where any parties are.

1169
00:52:45.540 --> 00:52:47.220
I was so boring, you know?

1170
00:52:47.220 --> 00:52:49.940
But all of a sudden, he thought I was a crazy, wacky gal.

1171
00:52:50.400 --> 00:52:53.420
Well, it sounds like you kind of had a good relationship with him, at leaSt.

1172
00:52:53.920 --> 00:52:54.480
Did you?

1173
00:52:54.700 --> 00:52:55.180
Sort of?

1174
00:52:55.520 --> 00:52:57.740
Or did it become a burden like it is for Andy?

1175
00:52:58.000 --> 00:52:59.200
No, it was a total burden.

1176
00:52:59.200 --> 00:53:03.580
I would like hide from him in the hallway because he would expect me to say something wacky or crazy.

1177
00:53:03.860 --> 00:53:10.460
And I'm like, listen, just because I played a zany newscaster or, you know, the nervous laugh neighbor

1178
00:53:10.460 --> 00:53:14.300
doesn't mean I'm going to be that when I just want to go to the bathroom.

1179
00:53:15.160 --> 00:53:16.300
Yeah, I get it.

1180
00:53:16.360 --> 00:53:20.880
Please don't expect me to be a character when I'm at the vending machine or just trying to go pee.

1181
00:53:21.500 --> 00:53:26.860
You know, folder guy who sent me to the airport FedEx that one evening?

1182
00:53:27.820 --> 00:53:30.280
I really didn't care for him.

1183
00:53:30.340 --> 00:53:32.660
And I did snark him out one day.

1184
00:53:32.800 --> 00:53:33.280
You did?

1185
00:53:33.380 --> 00:53:34.520
And it was really liberating.

1186
00:53:35.080 --> 00:53:39.840
As you can probably surmise, he was a very controlling personality type.

1187
00:53:40.340 --> 00:53:44.180
And I was working at an office that was very contained.

1188
00:53:44.540 --> 00:53:46.080
You couldn't leave for lunch.

1189
00:53:46.220 --> 00:53:47.180
There was nothing around.

1190
00:53:47.180 --> 00:53:49.160
It was a very industrial area.

1191
00:53:49.300 --> 00:53:51.580
So you had to eat in their cafeteria.

1192
00:53:52.060 --> 00:53:54.020
And there was a little outdoor courtyard.

1193
00:53:54.020 --> 00:53:56.920
And his office looked out over the outdoor courtyard.

1194
00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:57.820
He had a window.

1195
00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:00.920
He could see everybody out his window.

1196
00:54:01.480 --> 00:54:06.980
So one day after lunch, I only got a half hour lunch, by the way, unpaid.

1197
00:54:07.320 --> 00:54:08.500
I'd like to say that.

1198
00:54:08.700 --> 00:54:11.460
I did not get to put that half hour on my time card.

1199
00:54:11.980 --> 00:54:17.500
He called me into his office and he said, I was watching you during lunch.

1200
00:54:18.040 --> 00:54:18.480
Ew!

1201
00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:19.260
Mm-hmm.

1202
00:54:19.700 --> 00:54:22.280
He said, I noticed that you put your head down on the table.

1203
00:54:22.560 --> 00:54:22.920
I don't know.

1204
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:24.940
Maybe you were taking a little nap.

1205
00:54:25.520 --> 00:54:26.760
And I said, I did.

1206
00:54:26.940 --> 00:54:27.780
I was tired.

1207
00:54:27.780 --> 00:54:32.180
After I ate, I laid my head down and I closed my eyes.

1208
00:54:32.180 --> 00:54:33.100
It's a nice day out.

1209
00:54:33.160 --> 00:54:33.900
I felt the sunshine.

1210
00:54:33.900 --> 00:54:34.840
It felt really good.

1211
00:54:35.160 --> 00:54:36.440
He said, yeah, you know what?

1212
00:54:36.440 --> 00:54:37.680
That's really unprofessional.

1213
00:54:38.080 --> 00:54:40.400
This isn't a place to take a nap.

1214
00:54:40.400 --> 00:54:41.600
This is a workplace.

1215
00:54:42.800 --> 00:54:43.520
Oh, my God.

1216
00:54:43.660 --> 00:54:44.340
What did you say?

1217
00:54:44.720 --> 00:54:49.980
I said, well, since you're not paying me for my half hour lunch, I'm going to do whatever

1218
00:54:49.980 --> 00:54:50.520
I want.

1219
00:54:51.200 --> 00:54:55.840
I said, if you'd like to pay me for that time, then you can give me instructions on how to

1220
00:54:55.840 --> 00:54:56.220
behave.

1221
00:54:56.440 --> 00:55:02.780
But otherwise, I'll do whatever I'd like during my half hour of unpaid time here in this building

1222
00:55:02.780 --> 00:55:03.800
that I can't leave.

1223
00:55:04.460 --> 00:55:05.800
And then I walked out.

1224
00:55:06.480 --> 00:55:07.460
I love it.

1225
00:55:07.800 --> 00:55:09.360
Because I'd kind of had enough.

1226
00:55:09.940 --> 00:55:16.100
I was like, I'll make your multiple copies for your dumb colored folders and I'll drive

1227
00:55:16.100 --> 00:55:19.820
your last minute work that you couldn't get around to down to the airport.

1228
00:55:20.580 --> 00:55:26.320
But because of all that, I'm going to need to lay my head down at lunchtime because you're

1229
00:55:26.320 --> 00:55:28.580
a major headache in my life and I need a second.

1230
00:55:30.940 --> 00:55:32.000
I love that.

1231
00:55:32.160 --> 00:55:32.800
I love it.

1232
00:55:33.600 --> 00:55:37.540
Oh, here's the thing I knew in that moment.

1233
00:55:37.760 --> 00:55:43.660
I knew that he couldn't fire me because I knew he didn't want to train someone new to

1234
00:55:43.660 --> 00:55:45.160
do all of his weird folder.

1235
00:55:46.040 --> 00:55:52.700
And so I had the tiniest bit of agency and I cashed it in in that moment.

1236
00:55:52.700 --> 00:55:57.200
And I'm glad I did because the look on his face was priceless.

1237
00:55:57.220 --> 00:55:59.440
And I still think back to it today.

1238
00:55:59.680 --> 00:56:00.840
He was speechless.

1239
00:56:01.820 --> 00:56:04.080
He did not know how to respond to that.

1240
00:56:06.180 --> 00:56:07.200
Oh, my gosh.

1241
00:56:07.400 --> 00:56:12.180
I don't know how this turned into stories about our early days working.

1242
00:56:12.520 --> 00:56:14.540
But apparently we needed to get this out.

1243
00:56:14.700 --> 00:56:15.560
It's therapeutic, Jenna.

1244
00:56:15.740 --> 00:56:17.200
We're talking about all of our old bosses.

1245
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:18.240
I feel better.

1246
00:56:18.460 --> 00:56:19.180
I do, too.

1247
